A||N||5||Will||2.5 turn rack?||||1||
Z||000000||Will||05-08-2001||03:26 PM||||In my opinion, the 3 turn rack on my 87 GT is too slow. Does anyone know of any steering rack, power or otherwise, that can be swapped in without much hassle?<BR>I searched, and came up with this thread: <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/007069.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/007069.html</A>  in which rockcrawl talks about using a Corvette and possibly a Merkur rack. The Corvette rack sounds like it has too many dimensional incompatibilities to me. What aobut the Merkur rack? Others?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||rockcrawl||05-08-2001||05:25 PM||||Will,<BR> I haven't had time to work on mine, so no further updates. I have talked to a few guys who have sucessfully used Chevette racks for power steering, but I don't know what the turns ratio is. To mount the Chevette rack, one of the mounts needs to be cut off, moved, and re-welded on the crossmember. One or both of the tie rods need to be lengthened. The steering shaft coupler needs to be changed. I still haven't located a XR4 rack to experiment with.<P>Jon||||reg||1
Z||000002||84Bill||05-08-2001||06:11 PM||||what happend to all the 88 cars that had P/S racks removed at the dealers prior to sale? Obviously there were some made. Just wondering who made them and for what cars. Fiero only item?||||reg||1
Z||000003||MrPBody||05-08-2001||07:57 PM||||Maybe I'm making this up . . .<P>I think AusFiero raised the possibility that a Volvo rack could be used.<P>I also vaguely remember that IMSA Fieros had a 2.5-turn rack.  Must have been a bugger to steer at low speed.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Oreif||05-08-2001||08:01 PM||||The stock Fiero rack is a 9 to 1 ratio. (3 turns lock to lock) IRM use to sell the Indy Fiero rack, (IMSA rack) which was 16 to 1 (2.5 turns lock to lock) Not sure if they still do. When I get home I'll look in the Fiero Race car book and see who makes the racing rack.||||reg||1
Z||000005||rockcrawl||05-08-2001||08:05 PM||||I don't think any of the '88s made it as far as the dealer with the power steering. I believe they were removed before they left the factory. Finding an '88 power rack would be about as easy as finding an '89 Fiero.<P>Hmmm... The volvo rack, I almost forgot about that one. Yet another possibility.<P>||||reg||1
